{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3461","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3461","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3461\",\"parent_revision\":\"aaa6e084612d1111c0a21ad483770b920c63194369bcf360fd7a6745286f4606\",\"root_revision\":\"aaa6e084612d1111c0a21ad483770b920c63194369bcf360fd7a6745286f4606\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAn agent or contributor reading these files cannot interpret them without an external lookup that may no longer resolve. For the third item the cost is larger: the suite can pass while the system diverges from what the architecture says it should do, which is the failure mode the architecture document exists to prevent.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Was Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThree pre-existing violations of rules the repository has now established: that documentation states what is true now, that nothing links to a deliberation document, and that system and end-to-end tests are written against the architecture rather than the code.\\n\\n### 1. Issue numbers embedded in test docstrings and source comments\\n\\nTest docstrings across `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/` carry bare issue references \u2014 `#1770` in `test_drafting_state.py`, `test_large_document_write.py` and `test_server.py`, `#1725` in `test_server_mcp.py`, `#2509` in `test_gist_write_through.py`, `#715` in `test_readers/test_detect.py`, `#3432` in `test_consolidated_tools.py`, among others. `issues/3238` is repeated through `plugins/agentskill-kaizen/mcp/server.py`.\\n\\nA reader must resolve each pointer outside the file to interpret it, and the pointer goes stale without the file changing.\\n\\n### 2. The ADR filename convention embeds an issue number\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md` records the convention as `ADR-{issue}-{n}-{slug}.md`. Every ADR filename in the repository therefore carries a temporal reference in its own name, so this cannot be corrected without renaming files and updating whatever still resolves to them.\\n\\n### 3. Tests assert against implementation behaviour rather than a specification\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/dh_core/ledger_spec.py` with its closure tests, and `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_ledger_check_order.py` deriving its expectations from `CHECKS[command, from_status]`, are the pattern the repository wants: the test asserts against a declared specification, so a specification change reddens the test.\\n\\nOther test modules sampled during this session assert against implementation behaviour instead. A test written that way ratifies whatever the implementation happens to do, and drifts together with it \u2014 it cannot report that the design was wrong, because it was written after the design was chosen.\\n\\n**Not measured**: the proportion of the suite that does this. It was stated as \\\"most of the suite\\\" during the session; that quantifier was asserted without being measured and should not be carried forward. Establishing the actual proportion is part of the work.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Where Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/`, `plugins/agentskill-kaizen/mcp/server.py`, `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md`, `plugins/development-harness/docs/adrs/`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n[#3050](https://github.com/Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills/issues/3050) is adjacent to the second item \u2014 it covers ADR identifiers referenced with no definition document, whereas this covers issue numbers embedded in ADR filenames. Related rather than duplicate; a groomer should read both before scoping either.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Note On Granularity\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCaptured as one item because it was reported as one. The third observation is architectural and much larger than the other two, which are hygiene, so this may want splitting at grooming.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ec706b4a5c0e6173470fdd0b8cafdbdd9f25af7518826747c697809294eaf459\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUIyhJQ\"}"}